519" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287385} {:answer/id #uuid "f263f1c5-c023-52c5-b17c-3b36f00f05e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287386} {:answer/id #uuid "8c4f07ea-3198-56ba-ae69-7e96fd25c5f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287387} {:answer/id #uuid "5ab376a3-3e60-5149-ae06-fc3d45c3c97f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c4f07ea-3198-56ba-ae69-7e96fd25c5f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287387} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e87eca0-e8ca-545a-beab-0c3a297aa01b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287383}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c9798ed5-9467-5b84-a966-140686dec581" :question/math-academy-id "q-79281" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/assets/ac2bba143473bc68e3a578c008a5de3cc36727d984bfba5d5e0da95462c08f77.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal radius $2$ and vertical radius $4,$ as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the ellipse once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(2,0)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the ellipse is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(a,0).$\n\nIn our case, $a=2$ and $b=4.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287389 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d82541c-40ca-5df9-aa17-c20b201fadd4" :knowledge-point/title "The Parametric Equations of an Ellipse Centered at a General Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddb11eed-bce0-582c-8842-6446c050a611" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4,\\,y=12\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287391} {:answer/id #uuid "c6b029aa-67e2-5872-81b1-4042ef2c3886" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4,\\,y=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287392} {:answer/id #uuid "6ab7c736-cbca-506e-87d1-c8c129a01ce8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287393} {:answer/id #uuid "96f048cd-e568-55a9-a7d4-58df0b098b50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +6,\\,y=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287394} {:answer/id #uuid "b07a6d14-baa0-58c8-b3e9-81f6bf4911cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +6,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ab7c736-cbca-506e-87d1-c8c129a01ce8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287393} :answer-field/id #uuid "23e286de-f5bc-569e-942f-9a935d1a8dd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "626d47b7-1134-59f0-a220-6a53e468dd6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-79289" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/assets/c7bb3c2ce6fe6fe2ea8c3a772b01077bb2fe4e40e005c05682989e8ea82ccc73.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse centered at $(4,6)$ with horizontal radius $8$ and vertical radius $6,$ as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the ellipse once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(12,6)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the point $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +h,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +k,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the ellipse is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(h+a,k).$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(4,6),$ $a=8$ and $b=6.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +6,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"}]}
